"hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2721,"Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) said: When the Prophet (PBUH) would wake up from sleep, he used to pray: ""Al-Hamdu Lillah-il-Dhi Ahiyana Ba'ad Ma'atana and ilahih an-Nushur."" All praise is due to Allah Who raised us up after sleep and to Him we must return."
2722,"Sayyidina Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrated the hadith that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Whoever wakes up at night and recites: “There is no god but Allah. All praises belong to Him, and His Self is pure, and there is no god but Allah, and no one has the power to avoid sins or to do good without Allah's help. Then he should say: ""O Allah! Forgive me"" or he should say, ""If someone makes dua, then his prayer will be accepted."""
2723,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abazai said on the authority of his father Sayyiduna Abazaa, may Allah be pleased with him: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would wake up in the morning, he would say: The religion of peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and the nation of his father Ibrahim Hanif and Muslim."
2724,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me what should I say when it is morning or evening? He said: ""Say: ""Allah, the Creator of the Heavens . From the evil of Satan and his polytheism.” 
 The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Recite this dua when it is morning and evening, and recite it when you go to bed."""
2725,"On the authority of Mu'adh bin Anas, his father said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever, while wearing a new cloth, says: ""Al-hamdu lillah-il-dhi-ki-kasani-ha-za-wa-razaqaniyah-min-ghayr-i-haul-mini-wala-wala"
2726,"Sayyidna Abu Hameed (RA) or Sayyidna Abu Aseed (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “When one of you enters the mosque, he should say: “Allahum aftah li abuwaab Rahmatik” (O Allah! Open the doors of Your mercy for me). And when he leaves the mosque, he should say:"
2727,"Muhammad bin Wasee said: I came to Makkah and met my (religious) brother Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar, so he told me about his father Abdullah. ""There is no god but Allah, He alone, He has no partner, His is the country, All praises are for Him, He gives life and He gives death, He is the Ever-Living, All good is in His hand, and He is Able to do all things."" 
 He said: ""Whoever says this, Allah Ta'ala will write for him a thousand thousand good deeds and erase a thousand thousand (i.e. one million) bad deeds and raise him a thousand and a thousand ranks."" 
 The narrator said: I went to Khorasan and met Qutiba bin Muslim and I said that I have brought a gift for you, so I narrated this hadith to him, after that he would ride his horse to the market, stand there and recite this dua and return (so that this great reward is obtained)."
2728,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Put a name on my name, do not put a surname on my surname."""
2729,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, you will be called by your names and the names of your fathers, so keep your names good."""
2730,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."""
2731,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Samrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade us to name our slaves these four names: Aflah, Nafi, Rabah, and Nijah."
2732,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may God be pleased with him) that Sayyidah Umm Asim (may God be pleased with him) whose name was Asiya (disobedient), the Prophet (peace be upon him) changed her name to Jamila."
2733,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The name of Sayyid Zainab (RA) was Bara (the most virtuous), the Prophet (PBUH) changed it to Zainab."
2734,"It was narrated on the authority of Tufail, the brother of Ayesha, that one of the polytheists said to one of the Muslims: You people are very good. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard this, he said: ""Do not say what Allah wills and Muhammad wills, instead say: What Allah wills, then Muhammad also wills."""
2735,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Do not call the vineyard Karam, because Karam is a Muslim man."""
2736,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: A slave was walking with the wives of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""O Anjaza! Take the glasses (glasses) and walk slowly."""
2737,"Bahz bin Hakim narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: ""Woe to the person who tells lies to make people laugh, woe to him, woe to him."""
2738,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confirmed the verses of Umayya bin Abi al-Salat in which he said: 
 Saturn and Thor are under his right foot and Nasr is under his left foot and Laith Satara is under his supervision. 
 The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Truthfully (i.e. all these planets are below Allah and Allah is above)"", then he said: 
 And when the sun rises at the end of every night, its color is red-pink. (i.e. because of greatness and glory). 
 He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is also true"" (It is in the hadith that the sun prostrates to Allah every day in the morning and asks for permission to rise, then it rises until Allah does not allow it on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be ordered to rise from where it sets... 
 Then someone said: 
 The sun refuses to rise of its own accord unless it is arrested in torment, chained. 
 The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""He spoke the truth."""
2739,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abi bin Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There is wisdom in poetry."""
2740,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""If one of you fills his stomach with pus and blood, it is better than if he fills it with poetry."""
2741,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Allah, the Exalted, bestows the understanding of religion on whomever He wishes to improve."""
2742,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Health and leisure are two of the blessings of God that most people do not value."""
2743,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever listens to people who do not like him, lead will be melted in his ears on the Day of Resurrection."""
2744,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not look behind the gaze (i.e., if you catch a glimpse of a strange woman unintentionally for the first time, do not look at her again) because the first glance is forgiven, but the second glance is a sin on you."""
2745,"Sayyidna Sufyan bin Abdullah al-Thaqfi said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something about Islam so that I don't ask anyone else about it. He said: ""Fear Allah and be steadfast."" I said: Then what is after that? So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed to his tongue (i.e. control it and guard it)."
2746,"Sayyiduna Sufyan bin Abdullah (RA) said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something I can hold on to. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Say Allah is my Lord, then rest on Him."" Then I said: O Messenger of Allah! What do you fear more than me? Sayyiduna Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held his tongue and said: ""His."""
2747,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! Which Islam is better? (That is, who is the best among the Muslims?) He said: ""From whose tongue and hand other Muslims should be safe."""
